<title>UK: PORTUGAL'S PETROGAL TO LIFT 11,000 BPD IRAQ OIL.</title>
<headline>PORTUGAL'S PETROGAL TO LIFT 11,000 BPD IRAQ OIL.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portguese state oil firm Petrogal expects to lift around 11,000 barrels per day (bpd) of Iraqi crude later this year under the U.N. oil-for-food programme, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The company will lift one cargo of one million barrels of Iraq's Kirkuk sour grade around September 25-30 from the Turkish port of Ceyhan, the traders said.</p>
<p>The company will not lift any of the crude in the remainder of the first 90-day period of the second phase of the programme which expires in early September.</p>
<p>The company lifted 11,000 bpd of Kirkuk in the first 180-day period of the programme.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
